        -:   37:/**
        -:   38: * A quick note on layer IDs:
        -:   39: *
        -:   40: * The layers are stored in separate enums so that certain functions can
        -:   41: * take in the enums as data types and don't have to know about layers from
        -:   42: * other applications.
        -:   43: *
        -:   44: * Layers that are shared between applications should be in the GAL_LAYER_ID enum.
        -:   45: *
        -:   46: * The PCB_LAYER_ID struct must start at zero for compatibility with legacy board files.
        -:   47: *
        -:   48: * Some functions accept any layer ID, so they start at zero (i.e. F_Cu) and go up to
        -:   49: * the LAYER_ID_COUNT, which needs to be kept up-to-date if new enums are added.
        -:   50: */
        -:   51:
        -:   52:
        -:   53:/**
        -:   54: * This is the definition of all layers used in Pcbnew.
        -:   55: *
        -:   56: * The PCB layer types are fixed at value 0 through #LAYER_ID_COUNT to ensure compatibility
        -:   57: * with legacy board files.
        -:   58: */
